 "post": {
  "title": "Why Scary Dates Work #shorts",
  "description": "Theo tells Milo to make his first date scary. In 1974, Donald Dutton and Arthur Aron had a woman interview men on the swaying Capilano Suspension Bridge (about 70 m above the river) or a solid, low bridge, and give them her number in case they had questions. About half the men from the shaky bridge called her, versus roughly one in eight from the solid one. Psychologists call it misattribution of arousal: the racing heart came from the bridge, but it felt like attraction. #psychology #shorts #dating #attraction",
